  1516	def verify_capture(root, entry, commit, name):
  1517	    """True iff `entry` claims a captured transcript that is genuinely THIS
  1518	    commit's / THIS reviewer's committed log and whose sha256 matches.
  1519	
  1520	    Applies to BOTH transcript sources — "captured" (the tool ran the reviewer)
  1521	    and "attached" (an existing transcript was attested via --codex-log/--glm-log;
  1522	    same binding rules, minus the exit-code check the tool can't know).
  1523	
  1524	    The `source: "captured"` string alone means nothing — a hand-edited report
  1525	    could set it. Real transcript evidence must:
  1526	      * name the transcript EXACTLY `.coverloop/reports/<commit>.<name>.log`
  1527	        (no traversal, and no REPLAY of an old/unrelated log under a different
  1528	        commit or reviewer);
  1529	      * resolve — after following any symlinks — to a real file INSIDE the
  1530	        reports dir (a symlink pointing outside is rejected);
  1531	      * hash to the recorded digest (catches tampering).
