  1832	
  1833	    Provenance (R3): the evidence report is bound to a commit hash, but a hash
  1834	    alone doesn't prove WHO authored it. We require `git log %G?` == "G" — a good
  1835	    signature from a trusted key (gpg owner-trust, or ssh allowed_signers) — so
  1836	    unreviewed code can't be laundered onto an unsigned/forged/untrusted-key
  1837	    commit and gated green. Opt-in (--require-signed-commit); never changes the
  1838	    default path. errors='replace' so a non-UTF-8 signer name can't raise a
  1839	    ValueError past the OSError handler (GLM R3 P2-1). Fail-closed.
  1840	
  1841	    signers_file (R4 / Sol gap #2): when given, verify against a REPO-COMMITTED
  1842	    ssh allowed_signers policy (via -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile) instead of
  1843	    each machine's ambient git trust — so a project defines WHO may sign,
  1844	    uniformly across machines and CI. Commit the file so it's authoritative in a
  1845	    clean checkout (same trust model as the rest of .coverloop)."""
