  2270	        "PASS WITH RISKS", no lowercase, no "APPROVE";
  2271	      * the last one is among the final `tail_lines` non-empty lines, so it is
  2272	        the reviewer's closing word rather than something near the top.
  2273	
  2274	    The whole transcript is read, not a tail window: a review that says FAIL and
  2275	    then emits 5 KB of appendix would otherwise have its failure scroll out of
  2276	    view. The closing-position rule is the other half of the same idea — a
  2277	    prompt echo containing the marker, followed by a review that never reaches a
  2278	    verdict, must not count as approval. The small allowance exists because real
  2279	    reviewers append a footer (Codex prints "tokens used" and a count after its
  2280	    reply); it is not room for review content.
  2281	    """
  2282	    lines = (text or "").splitlines()
  2283	    live = [(i, ln.strip()) for i, ln in enumerate(lines) if ln.strip()]
  2284	    markers = [(n, body) for n, (i, body) in enumerate(live) if _VERDICT_MARKER.match(lines[i])]
  2285	    if not markers:
  2286	        return "fail"
  2287	    if any(body != _VERDICT_CANONICAL_PASS for _n, body in markers):
  2288	        return "fail"
  2289	    if len(live) - markers[-1][0] > tail_lines:
  2290	        return "fail"          # a marker buried above the review is not a verdict
  2291	    return "pass"
